# richPort — front-end environment
#
# Copy to .env for local development. On Vercel, set the same names under
# Settings → Environment Variables. Everything here ships to the browser:
# VITE_ prefixed values are inlined into the bundle at build time, so never
# put a secret in this file.

# Where testimonials and booking requests are stored.
# Project → Settings → API in the Supabase dashboard.
# The anon key is designed to be public — what it can do is decided by the
# row-level security policies in supabase/schema.sql, not by keeping it
# hidden. Run that file once in the SQL editor before the forms will work.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The retired Express backend. Left empty on purpose: the site no longer
# needs it, and anything still pointing here fails over to Supabase or to a
# send-it-yourself fallback. Set it only if that server is ever revived.
VITE_AUTH_ENDPOINT=
